  "caption": "Quinn took up horse riding, walked out like a cowboy, and then the low back joined in.\n\nRiding means absorbing every bump, often in a slightly lopsided position, so low back, hips, groin, sitting bones and neck can ache. Back ache after riding often isn't a spine problem. Falls are the bigger risk.\n\nWhat can help: trunk and back endurance work off the horse, hip mobility, single-leg and glute exercises to even out asymmetry, general fitness, and a helmet on every ride, plus considering a body protector.\n\nAfter any fall with a head knock, don't ride again that day. Get checked for neck or back concerns after a fall or a limb you can't move.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
